.TH CY 8 "2027" "KythOS Kernal" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
cy \- manage authenticated distribution packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cy
.RI [ options ] " command " [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
cy is the KythOS Kernal operator interface to the packaged APT backend.
Commands that change system packages require an authenticated administrator.
Repository identities and backend version information retain their provenance.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B update
Refresh signed repository package indexes.
.TP
.B upgrade
Install available package upgrades.
.TP
.B full-upgrade
Upgrade packages, allowing the backend to resolve dependency changes.
.TP
.B install
Install named repository packages and their dependencies.
.TP
.B remove
Remove named packages.
.TP
.B autoremove
Review and remove dependencies the backend considers no longer required.
.TP
.B search
Find packages by words in repository metadata.
.TP
.B show
Read repository metadata for a package.
.TP
.B list
List package records. Use --installed or --upgradable to narrow the list.
.TP
.B help
Show KythOS command examples.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show KythOS command examples.
.TP
.B --version
Report the packaged backend version and provenance.
.TP
.B --simulate
Preview an action using the backend's simulation mode.
.TP
.B --assume-yes
Supply the backend's affirmative-answer option.
.TP
.B --quiet
Request quieter backend output.
.TP
.B --installed
Limit list output to installed packages.
.TP
.B --upgradable
Limit list output to packages with available upgrades.
.SH NOTES
cy blocks configuration injection, package-authentication bypasses, and local
package or URI operands. The ordinary packaged backend remains available for
compatibility and administrative workflows outside this interface.
Inspect a proposed transaction before accepting package removals.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo cy update
cy list --upgradable
sudo cy install package-name
cy --simulate autoremove
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR kythos-help (1)
